# ==============================================================================
# Victoria Metrics Configuration Template
# ==============================================================================
# This template generates command-line arguments for the Victoria Metrics server.
# It is intended to be used in conjunction with a systemd unit file or a wrapper
# script that passes these ARGS to the `victoria-metrics` binary.
#
# Self-Documentation:
# - Each directive is prefixed with a comment derived from the schema description.
# - Variables use the `| default()` filter to ensure safe rendering even if undefined.
# - No arbitrary Python or non-standard filters are used.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ARGS: The base set of command-line arguments for the Victoria Metrics server.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Due to shell escaping rules, backslashes for regexes must be doubled (\\d for \d).
# If running under systemd, escaping may need to be quadrupled depending on
# how the service file interprets the ExecStart line.
#
# Variable: storage_data_path
# Description: The path to the directory where Victoria Metrics stores its data.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARGS="-storageDataPath={{ (storage_data_path | default('/var/lib/victoria-metrics')) | string }}"